{
  "study": "TII-CEE-1",
  "milestone": "M1",
  "notes": [
    "The training track's fourth graph: graph_training_m3.json's stages unchanged, and E10's cohort-X integrity check (e10-cohort-x) after the five fold trainings and rollouts. Installed as $TII/pipeline/graph.json (tiicee/pipeline/graph.py). The loader ignores the keys 'notes' and 'note'.",
    "Gate G_resume (gates/resume_gate.py) reads the Nemotron bench's approved report; every training stage waits on it, and a rollout is skipped with its training.",
    "E9's trainings follow the Granite bench (e9-bench-granite), whose approved report of November 13, 2026 read outcome ok with no recipe repair (RESEARCH_LEDGER.md).",
    "Every Granite stage binds the backbone overlay as role backbone_overlay (tiicee/clinical/backbone.py, chosen), so the file naming the backbone, its revision and the fixed system message is hashed with the stage's inputs. E9 trains and rolls out on E8's data: same split files, same 240 validation admissions.",
    "Every training binds its data directory: e8-data/out for E8 (train.csv, val.csv, lab_test_mapping.csv), a fold directory of e10-folds/out for E10 (also heldout.csv, which the training checks is disjoint and never trains on). No test.csv anywhere.",
    "A part ends at the planned epoch boundary or at Slurm's warning, and the next part resumes (tiicee/clinical/train.py). GPU estimates follow EXPERIMENT_CARDS/E8.md and E10.md; resources follow graph_training_m1.json's bench and rollout stages.",
    "Not here yet: the per-policy probe conformance of specification 10.1.",
    "Training stages ask for 16 GB of host memory: every Nemotron bench, rollout and training job of November 13, 2026 peaked at 6.4 to 7.0 GB (sacct MaxRSS, sstat), and the class QOS's shared 250 GB was what held them. An out-of-memory exit is retried at 1.5 times the memory. The Granite bench's four jobs peaked at 7.1 to 7.7 GB. E9's Granite trainings ask for 14 GB, about 1.8 times that peak.",
    "Training stages ask for 4 CPUs. Each training averages about one CPU (sstat AveCPU against elapsed time), but the only training started with 2, e10-train-f2 on November 13, 2026 at 5:26 PM EST, had not finished a backward pass after 50 minutes, its GPU busy and its main thread waiting on a device-to-host copy, while the trainings started with 4 had; it was cancelled and the request went back to 4 (RESEARCH_LEDGER.md, Operations, evening)."
  ],
  "stage_modules": [
    "tiicee.clinical.folds",
    "tiicee.clinical.train",
    "tiicee.clinical.rollout",
    "tiicee.clinical.bench",
    "tiicee.clinical.acceptance",
    "tiicee.clinical.cohort_x"
  ],
